MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_001: I watched you in battle, Simon. You're quite skilled.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_002: Thanks. I'm nothing special though.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_003: You need not be so humble. I know that they call\nyou the Sky-Drum.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_004: The beating of a drum through the skies—or thunder,\nin other words. It paints a captivating picture.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_005: There's a story there, y'know... I'd been sent in to\nhelp resolve some small-scale conflict.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_006: Our commander panicked and ordered a charge\ninto a valley where the enemy had set up shop.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_007: There was nothing to be done except follow the\norders we'd been given. We were wiped out.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_008: A foolish commander is a woeful thing. One error\ncan result in hundreds, or thousands, of lives lost.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_009: They were good men too. Fearless, all of them...
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_010: I survived by crawling through their corpses. But I'm\nnot one to just accept defeat.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_011: I hid halfway up a cliffside and waited for the enemy\nto pass on their way back to their camp.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_012: The moment their general got close enough, I jumped\nfrom the cliff and killed him in a few quick strokes.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_013: Then stole a horse and made a break for it during\nthe chaos. I took a few arrows, but it was worth it.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_014: And after that, folks started using those ridiculous\nnames for me, like Sky-Drum.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_015: I remember this story now. A sage of the forest\npeoples told me of a cliffside ambush.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_016: "He fell from the sky, and the sound of his impact\nwas like the echo of a war drum."
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_017: "The enemy general was split in half by the blow,"\nas if he were a tree struck by lightning.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_018: That's what they've been saying, is it? Heh... I don't\nrecall cutting him in half. Not all the way.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_019: So the tale stemmed from your exploits. You are as\nferocious as a Saraminian born and bred.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_020: If I have the favor of the queen herself, my star may\nbe on the rise.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_021: Have I mentioned my family is of Damascar blood?
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_022: I mean, not like a pureblood Saraminian, of course...
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_023: Intriguing. You have a rare courage, Simon. I am\nproud to call you my kin.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_C_024: "Kin," huh? Don't think I'd go that far...
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_001: We offer our souls and dedicate this fight to Yu Phas.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_002: Offering up souls, are you?
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_003: And what of it? As my kin, you ought to know the\nprayer by heart.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_004: My family weren't the praying sort.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_005: Honoring Yu Phas wasn't a practice our ancestors\npassed down.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_006: You are of Damascar blood and yet you do not revere\nYu Phas?
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_007: Mercenaries usually try to keep death at a distance.\nThough I suppose you think I'm a faithless ingrate.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_008: I do. Forgetting the kindness shown to our ancestors\nis a high crime. But your death would be a waste.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_009: So I shall merely detain you until we can carve\nproper reverence for Yu Phas into your bones.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_010: Hey, hey, no need for all that! You Saramis people...
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_011: You can threaten me all you want. It won't change\nwhat I believe.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_012: Hmph. Hahaha!
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_013: Do not be so gullible. I meant it in jest.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_014: Yeah... Didn't seem like much of a joke with that\nice-cold glare aimed at me.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_015: It was a test of your mettle as a mercenary. A serious\njest, if you will.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_016: A serious jest, huh? Not much of a jest, then, is it,\nYour Majesty?
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_017: Then by way of apology, I shall share my thoughts.\nI will not be forcing my beliefs onto anyone.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_018: Children of Damascar come in many forms. Some\nserve the empire; others worship the god Balor.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_019: And some, like your family, have left their homeland\nin order to preserve their bloodline.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_020: Saramis welcomes them all. For they have each\ninherited the spirit of our ancestors.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_021: Perhaps it could one day be a refuge for those who\nwish to return to their mother culture.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_022: I always found the blood-and-faith sort to be a bit\nstuck in their ways—and usually crooked.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_023: Not unlike that commander I told you about before...\nBut you seem different, more open-minded.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_024: Maybe if you'd been giving the orders back then,\nsome of my men would still be alive.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_025: If you would prefer it, you are free to settle in\nSaramis without changing your beliefs.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_026: A soldier of your skill would be a welcome leader—or\nan instructor. The courtiers would not dare complain.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_027: I'm honored you, the queen herself, would make such\nan offer.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_028: But I have to turn you down. I'm not cut out for the\nlife of a career soldier. I need my freedom.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_029: Such stubbornness. You would remain a mercenary\ndespite a direct invitation from a queen?
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_030: If you prefer, noble Sky-Drum, ours can be a paid\narrangement.
MID_SE_Seo_Sim_B_031: Now you're speaking my language. Next time there's\na war you need fought, just say the word.